v 3
d pdemeds: medication-class exposure from pharmacy and medical claims
d
d pdemeds  - flags medication classes from pharmacy dispensing claims in
d            user-defined windows around an index date: any use, fills,
d            days supplied, quantity, first/last fill, days covered,
d            proportion of days covered, and opioid MME (total, average
d            daily, peak). Built-in library of about 50 classes (opioids,
d            NSAIDs, gabapentinoids, benzodiazepines, antidepressants,
d            corticosteroids, bone agents, diabetes, anticoagulants, DMARDs,
d            cardiovascular, ...), editable through a CSV file.
d pbmeds   - provider-administered drugs and procedures from medical claims
d            by HCPCS/CPT code (biologic DMARDs, infusions, injectable
d            steroids, epidural steroid injections, IV bone agents), with an
d            option to combine results with pdemeds.
d pdemme   - morphine milligram equivalents per dispensed unit from generic
d            drug name and strength text (CDC 2022 or 2016 factors).
d
d Works with any claims or dispensing data that have the required fields:
d Medicare, commercial, Medicaid, health-system/EHR records. Default
d variable names are the CMS CCW Medicare names; every name can be set
d with an option. Requires Stata 16 or later. Contains no patient data.
d
d After installing,
d -net get pdemeds, from(https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BrookMartin/pdemeds/main/)-
d downloads the synthetic test suite (pdemeds_test.do) and CSV templates of
d the class libraries.
d
d Author: Brook I. Martin, PhD MPH, University of Utah
d Support: https://github.com/BrookMartin/pdemeds/issues
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261120
d License: MIT
d
f pdemeds.ado
f pdemeds.sthlp
f pbmeds.ado
f pbmeds.sthlp
f pdemme.ado
f pdemme.sthlp
f pdemeds_test.do
f pdemeds_classes.csv
f pbmeds_classes.csv
